# Alembic Database Migrations

## Setup (first time after cloning)

After seeding the database, it's automatically stamped as up-to-date.

If you have an existing database, stamp it manually:
```bash
cd backend
alembic stamp head
```

## When you modify models.py

1. Generate a migration:
```bash
cd backend
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Add new_column to users"
```

2. Review the generated file in `alembic/versions/`

3. Apply the migration:
```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

## Common commands

```bash
# Check current revision
alembic current

# Show migration history
alembic history

# Upgrade to latest
alembic upgrade head

# Downgrade one revision
alembic downgrade -1

# Downgrade to specific revision
alembic downgrade abc123
```
